Z||000000||Ozzy||05-28-2000||04:49 PM||||Hey Dude!<P>I e-mailed you but got no response. Is that address valid or am I just not <I>important</I> to you?????  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Headed for Utah next weekend. Sunday in fact. Kind of interesting too...I don't have a deal on the table yet, don't know anyone in Provo, don't have a house lined up...<P>Not used to doing things this way. My pregnant wife is being VERY understanding. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyway, I'm not worried about work. There are all kinds of fiber optic networks being built in Salt Lake, around Ogden etc. I'm just waiting to pick the right deal. <P>Looking forward to seeing Utah again. Lived there in '94 for awhile. Cheaper to live than Washington for sure. Nice people too. I'm not LDS, but folks were nice just the same.<P>I'm gonna drag the GT behind the Ryder truck. My nephew is driving the Coupe and I'm STILL trying to sell the '84. I would keep the '84 if I could but have no way to get it there with out coming back for it. I still want to take the power options from it and place them in the '88. If you know anyone coming to Washington soon....<P>Ozzy||||reg||2
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||05-28-2000||05:29 PM||||Here I am. <P>I got your e-mail and ment to responde, but I have been working on all the cars in my family. My wife's car had the alternator go out after I played with the battery for a few days for nothing. Then my grandma's 92 Cutlass Supreme needed new rear brake pads... turned out getting reman calipers(long story). Between work and keeping all these cars on the road I have lost track of everything.<P>Sorry bout that.<P>As soon as you get settled in give me a buzz and we can get together and shoot the $hit.<P>I hope you find a job(I'm sure you will... SLC is growing like mad). <P>My wife is LDS and her family is as well. Talk about the Black Sheep. I have long hair and don't know what the inside of a church looks like.<P>BTW: do you have a 4 wheeler? Utah and Idaho has some killer sand dunes. ||||reg||11
Z||000002||Ozzy||05-28-2000||06:10 PM||||There u are...<P>No 4 wheeler dude! Maybe I could turn the '84 into one.....hmmmmmmm...6" lift, chunky rubber, supercharger twinturboenginerebuildmoremoneyshitfromthe wifestufftoworkonwithnosparetime...aaaarrrrrgghhhhhhhhhhh! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I have an old TT500 thumper for all that kinda stuff. Maybe my Montgomery Wards ride on lawnmower w/ hydrostatic drive??? A whole 15 hp!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Anyway, will be dropping our stuff in a storage in Provo next Monday, then gotta go to the SCTE expo in Las Vegas for a couple of days then will be back to look for a place to rent. Will give you an e-mail when I get somewhat organized.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
